            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "compression": 0,
            "text": "{\"response\":\"**Physical AI** is a loosely‑used term that refers to artificial‑intelligence systems that operate **in the real, physical world** rather than only in simulation or on a computer screen.  \\nIn other words, “Physical AI” is AI that is **embodied, interactive, and sensor‑driven**—the kind of intelligence that controls a robot, a drone, a self‑driving car, or any device that must sense, decide, and act in the physical environment.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key characteristics\\n\\n| Aspect | What it means for Physical AI |\\n|--------|--------------------------------|\\n| **Embodiment** | The AI is attached to a body (robotic arm, humanoid robot, mobile platform, etc.) and must map internal states to physical actions. |\\n| **Perception** | Uses real‑world sensors (cameras, lidar, force sensors, microphones, etc.) to build an internal representation of the environment. |\\n| **Actuation** | Generates motor commands that move actuators, actuate valves, drive wheels, etc. |\\n| **Real‑time constraints** | Must process data and output commands within tight time budgets (milliseconds to seconds). |\\n| **Uncertainty & Noise** | Deals with sensor noise, actuation errors, and unpredictable dynamics that are absent in pure simulation. |\\n| **Learning & Adaptation** | Often uses reinforcement learning, imitation learning, or adaptive control to improve performance over time. |\\n| **Safety & Robustness** | Must guarantee safe operation around humans, other robots, and delicate equipment. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Where Physical AI shows up\\n\\n| Domain | Typical Physical AI application |\\n|--------|---------------------------------|\\n| **Robotics** | Pick‑and‑place, humanoid robots, collaborative robots (cobots), autonomous service robots. |\\n| **Autonomous Vehicles** | Self‑driving cars, trucks, drones, and underwater vessels. |\\n| **Manufacturing & Automation** | Adaptive assembly lines, smart factories, predictive maintenance. |\\n| **Healthcare** | Surgical robots, rehabilitation exoskeletons, patient monitoring systems. |\\n| **Consumer Electronics** | Smart home assistants that move (e.g., robotic vacuums, drones). |\\n| **Agriculture** | Autonomous tractors, crop‑monitoring drones, robotic harvesters. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Related research fields\\n\\n* **Embodied AI / Embodied Cognition** – The study of how body and environment shape intelligence.  \\n* **Robot Learning\",\"sources\":[],\"session_id\":\"chat-session-1767004571947-mmmtaw0za\",\"tokens_used\":null,\"retrieval_info\":null}"
          },
